subproblems.statement:
Let P, k ∈ ℕ, let g : ℝ^P → ℝ be a function, and let η : ℝ^P → Λ^k(ℝ^P) be a k-form, i.e. a map into the continuous alternating k-linear real forms on ℝ^P (DifferentialForm (Euclid P) k). Let x ∈ ℝ^P be a point at which both g and η are Fréchet differentiable. Then d(gη)(x) = g(x)·dη(x) + alternatizeUncurryFin((Dg(x)).smulRight(η(x))), where:
- gη is the k-form y ↦ g(y)·η(y);
- d = exteriorDerivative is Mathlib's extDeriv, so dθ(x) = alternatizeUncurryFin(fderiv ℝ θ x);
- Dg(x) = fderiv ℝ g x;
- (Dg(x)).smulRight(η(x)) is the continuous linear map v ↦ Dg(x)(v)·η(x).
The last term is dg∧η at x.
